Test builds no longer stamp a node freed into the pool, so a node freed
twice is taken twice without a report where ASan is off. Caught where the
node pool is on; the guard skips under ASan, which reports it itself.
Guarded-by: "alloc sweep: a key directory node freed twice ends the test build"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/btree.cppm b/bytecaskdb/btree.cppm
index 92b96c5..e27ac35 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/btree.cppm
+++ b/bytecaskdb/btree.cppm
@@ -196,12 +196,6 @@ public:
       if (s.free.size() < kMaxPooledNodes) {
         try {
           s.free.push_back(p);
-#ifdef BYTECASK_TESTING
-          // Only a node the pool keeps: its memory stays mapped, so a
-          // later check reads bytes the pool holds. One freed to operator
-          // delete is not stamped, and goes unchecked.
-          std::memcpy(p, &kFreedStamp, sizeof kFreedStamp);
-#endif
           return;
         } catch (...) {  // the list could not grow: free the node instead
         }
